        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Pyrolysis-gas chromatography (Py-GC) thermally decomposes complex samples into smaller volatile fragments, which are separated using GC.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PSI:MS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1002272"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Gas-liquid chromatography (GLC) employs an inert gaseous mobile phase and a liquid stationary phase immobilized on a solid support, separating volatile analytes by differential partitioning in the column.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:1003717</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>gas-liquid chromatography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Gas-liquid chromatography (GLC) employs an inert gaseous mobile phase and a liquid stationary phase immobilized on a solid support, separating volatile analytes by differential partitioning in the column.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PSI:MS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003718 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003718">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Non-polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography employs phases like polydimethylsiloxane (PDMS), where separation is based on analyte volatility and dispersion interactions, optimally retaining non-polar compounds.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:1003718</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>non-polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003718"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Non-polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography employs phases like polydimethylsiloxane (PDMS), where separation is based on analyte volatility and dispersion interactions, optimally retaining non-polar compounds.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PSI:MS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003719 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003719">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mid-polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography employs phases such as polysiloxanes, providing balanced separation through both dispersion and dipole interactions for analytes of intermediate polarity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:1003719</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>mid-polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003719"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Mid-polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography employs phases such as polysiloxanes, providing balanced separation through both dispersion and dipole interactions for analytes of intermediate polarity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PSI:MS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003720 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003720">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography uses stationary phases such as polyethylene glycol, maximizing retention and selectivity for polar analytes via dipole–dipole and hydrogen bonding interactions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:1003720</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003720"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Polar stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography uses stationary phases such as polyethylene glycol, maximizing retention and selectivity for polar analytes via dipole–dipole and hydrogen bonding interactions.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PSI:MS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003721 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003721">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003717"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Chiral stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography uses a stationary phase with bonded chiral selectors, enabling enantiomeric separation by stereoselective interactions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:1003721</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>chiral stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003721"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Chiral stationary phase gas-liquid chromatography uses a stationary phase with bonded chiral selectors, enabling enantiomeric separation by stereoselective interactions.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PSI:MS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003722 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1003722">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_1002272"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Gas-solid chromatography (GSC) separates volatile analytes by adsorption onto a solid stationary phase, with elution governed by analyte–surface interactions and adsorption.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:1003722</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>gas-solid chromatography</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
