        <owl:annotatedTarget>Molecular sieve stationary phase gas–solid chromatography separates volatile analytes by differential adsorption onto a porous, crystalline aluminosilicate solid phase, enabling selective separation of permanent gases and small hydrocarbons.</owl:annotatedTarget>
