        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Capillary electrophoresis (CE) is an electrophoretic separation technique performed in narrow-bore capillaries, in which analytes migrate through an electrolyte solution under the influence of an electric field and separate according to their electrophoretic mobility.</owl:annotatedTarget>
