            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The log ratios of successive TIC quantiles. A value triplet represents the original QuaMeter metrics, the log ratios of TIC-Q2 to TIC-Q1, TIC-Q3 to TIC-Q2, TIC-max to TIC-Q3. The number of values in the tuple implies the quantile mode.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>MS</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MS1-TIC-Q2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MS1-TIC-Q3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MS1-TIC-Q4</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>MS:4000187</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>The metric informs about the dynamic range of the acquisition along the chromatographic separation. The ratios provide information on the distribution of the TIC values for one LC-MS run. Within an experiment, with the same LC setup, values should be comparable between samples.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>MS1 TIC quantile ratios</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MS_4000187"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The log ratios of successive TIC quantiles. A value triplet represents the original QuaMeter metrics, the log ratios of TIC-Q2 to TIC-Q1, TIC-Q3 to TIC-Q2, TIC-max to TIC-Q3. The number of values in the tuple implies the quantile mode.</owl:annotatedTarget>
